Article 9 The Housing Provident Fund Management Committee shall perform the following duties in the management of the housing provident fund:
(1) Formulate and adjust specific management measures for the housing provident fund in accordance with relevant laws, regulations, and policies, and supervise their implementation;
(2) Draft the specific deposit ratio of the housing provident fund in accordance with the provisions of Article 18 of these Regulations;
(3) Determine the maximum loan amount of the housing provident fund;
(4) Examine and approve the plan for collection and use of the housing provident fund;
(5) Deliberate the distribution plan of the value-added income from the housing provident fund;
(6) Examine and approve the report on the implementation of the plan for collection and use of the housing provident fund.

Article 11 The Housing Provident Fund Management Center shall perform the following duties:
(1) Formulate and implement the plan for collection and use of the housing provident fund;
(2) Be responsible for recording the deposit, withdrawal, use, and other circumstances of employees' housing provident fund;
(3) Be responsible for the accounting of the housing provident fund;
(4) Examine and approve the withdrawal and use of the housing provident fund;
(5) Be responsible for the preservation and repayment of the housing provident fund;
(6) Prepare a report on the implementation of the plan for collection and use of the housing provident fund;
(7) Undertake other matters decided by the Housing Provident Fund Management Committee.

Article 23 The housing provident fund deposited by a unit for its employees shall be listed as expenditure in accordance with the following provisions:
(1) For state organs, it shall be listed as expenditure in the budget;
(2) For public institutions, after the financial department verifies their revenues and expenditures, it shall be listed as expenditure in the budget or expenses;
(3) For enterprises, it shall be listed as expenditure in the cost.

Article 24 An employee may withdraw the balance stored in his or her housing provident fund account under any of the following circumstances:
(1) Purchasing, constructing, renovating, or carrying out major repair of self-occupied housing;
(2) Retiring or retiring for rest;
(3) Totally losing the ability to work and terminating the labor relationship with the unit;
(4) Leaving the country for permanent residence;
(5) Repaying the principal and interest of a housing loan;
(6) Where the rent exceeds the prescribed proportion of the family's wage income.
Where an employee withdraws the housing provident fund in accordance with items (2), (3), and (4) of the preceding paragraph, the employee's housing provident fund account shall be closed at the same time.
Where an employee dies or is declared dead, the employee's successor or legatee may withdraw the balance stored in the employee's housing provident fund account; if there is no successor or legatee, the balance stored in the employee's housing provident fund account shall be included in the value-added income of the housing provident fund.

Article 34 The Housing Provident Fund Management Center and employees shall have the right to urge the unit to fulfill the following obligations in a timely manner:
(1) Registration for deposit, modification, or cancellation of registration of the housing provident fund;
(2) Opening, transfer, or sealing up of housing provident fund accounts;
(3) Depositing the housing provident fund in full.

Article 40 Where the Housing Provident Fund Management Center violates the provisions of these Regulations by committing any of the following acts, the competent administrative department of construction under the State Council or the competent administrative department of construction of the people's government of the province or autonomous region shall, in accordance with its administrative functions and powers, order it to make corrections within a specified time limit; the persons in charge who are liable and other directly responsible persons shall be given administrative sanctions according to law:
(1) Failing to establish a special account for the housing provident fund as required;
(2) Failing to examine and approve the withdrawal and use of the housing provident fund by employees as required;
(3) Failing to use the value-added income from the housing provident fund as required;
(4) Entrusting an institution other than the bank designated by the Housing Provident Fund Management Committee to handle the financial business of the housing provident fund;
(5) Failing to establish a subsidiary ledger of employees' housing provident fund;
(6) Failing to issue valid certificates of housing provident fund deposit to employees who deposit the housing provident fund;
(7) Failing to use the housing provident fund to purchase government bonds as required.
